WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.850
It’s been 10 years since the original MacBook
Air was released, and the design hasn’t

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.059
changed a single time, until now.

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:16.230
Apple’s new 2018 MacBook Air has been completely
redesigned to look more like their 12” MacBook,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.330
and it all looks great, except for a few problems
that are keeping me from ordering one right

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.330
this second.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.590
People bought the MacBook Air because it was
the cheapest way to get a reliable Apple laptop,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.189
along with the fact that it’s thin, light,
it’s loaded with ports and it’s got great

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:29.210
battery life.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.660
The biggest problem with the 2018 MacBook
Air is that it now costs $200 more, making

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.350
it only $100 cheaper than the 12” MacBook
and 13” MacBook Pro.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.420
Now while I agree that the MacBook Air is
better than the 12” MacBook in basically

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.330
every way except being a little thicker and
weight a little bit more, the 13” MacBook

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.190
Pro has a few pretty big advantages which
I’ll talk about in a minute.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:01:00.390
Apple really should have priced this at $1099
maximum, making the price gap $200 instead.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.450
Onto the second problem, there are now only
2 Thunderbolt 3 ports instead of the variety

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.740
of ports that came with the old MacBook Air,
which made it so attractive to regular users.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:12.009
Now, those same users have to go out and buy
adapters for all of their legacy devices,

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:15.420
even something as simple as using a flash
drive will require an adapter.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:22.890
Yes, Thunderbolt 3 is really nice since you
can connect powerful drives and a 5K display,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.259
but the market of regular users who just want
Apple’s cheapest MacBook don’t really

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:31.079
need all of that extra power like professional
users do, who are going to buying the MacBook

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:33.639
Pro anyways.

00:01:33.639 --> 00:01:42.609
Overall, a lot of the MacBook Airs’ target
market is going to have issues with the USB-C

00:01:42.609 --> 00:01:43.609
ports.

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:47.549
Now onto the third problem, the new MacBook
Air is still packing a dual-core processor

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:53.159
while the rest of the market is moving towards
quad-core processors.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:02:03.139
Yes, it can turbo-boost up to the same clock
speed as the base 13” MacBook Pro, but the

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.359
core speed is slower, and it’s only a 7w
chip instead of 15w on the Pro.

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:11.340
This means that the year-old 13” MacBook
Pro will still be faster than the new MacBook

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.340
Air.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.900
Not only that, but graphics performance is
even worse.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.989
In fact, the MacBook Pro’s graphics is over
50% faster than on the new MacBook Air.

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:25.909
Of course, that’s why it’s the MacBook
Pro, but if you check B&amp;H, it’s only $50

00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:27.079
more than the new MacBook Air.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.140
Apple could have easily added a 4-core processor
upgrade option to make users happy.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:34.159
Yes, the target market doesn’t really need
the extra power, but the only reason I haven’t

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:36.450
ordered the Air already is the lack of performance,
and I’m sure I’m not alone.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:40.909
For the 4th reason, even though the new MacBook
Air gets a retina display, it’s actually

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:43.780
worse than the 13” MacBook Pros retina display.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.450
The Pro gets a brighter, 500 nit display which
really helps for using it outside in the daylight

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.219
or even in a really bright room.

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:55.290
The Pro also gets P3 wide-color gamut support,
so it’s got much better color accuracy compared

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.290
to the Air.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:00.249
This is yet another reason to choose the Pro
over the Air, and you only have to pay $50

00:03:00.249 --> 00:03:01.249
more.

00:03:01.249 --> 00:03:05.569
For the 5th and final problem, the new MacBook
Air is still using Bluetooth 4.2 technology.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:10.010
Basically every single 2018 Apple device except
for the budget iPad has now moved on to Bluetooth

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:16.189
5, including all of the new iPhones, the HomePod,
the Apple TV 4K, the Mac Mini, the MacBook

00:03:16.189 --> 00:03:18.019
Pros and the new iPad Pro.

00:03:18.019 --> 00:03:21.620
Since everything else is moving forward with
Bluetooth 5.0, it sucks that Apple decided

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:26.069
to keep the MacBook Air at 4.2, but it’s
not as big of an issue as everything else,

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:38.670
since there aren’t that many Bluetooth 5
devices yet.

